<title>SOUTH AFRICA: ABN, BOE Natwest win Reuters S.African rand survey.</title>
<headline>ABN, BOE Natwest win Reuters S.African rand survey.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>ABN Amro Bank and BOE Natwest Securities in Johannesburg are the first joint winners in the Reuters Quarterly Survey after their economists correctly forecast the rand/dollar exchange rate at the end of 1996.</p>
<p>ABN economist Anastasia Gekis and BOE Natwest chief economist Nick Barnardt correctly forecast in November that the rand would end 1996 at 4.68 to the dollar.</p>
<p>The next survey will be carried out after the 1997/98 Budget is presented on March 13.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
</text>
